{
  // Benjamin's rule (goals/atoms, decision "atoms A1"): "Also no react hooks where effect/reactivity +
  // @effect/react-atom should can be used." and "useEffect banned with no exceptions." A web package extends this once
  // its state has moved to atoms; at the end every package does, the vendored kit (packages/ui/src/components,
  // packages/ui/src/hooks) excepted. What stays: the hooks of @effect/atom-react, useRef for a DOM node only (not
  // checkable here; `rg useRef` in the PLAN), useId, useDeferredValue and useTransition. A namespace import of react is
  // refused too, and so is the default import, so React.useEffect cannot be reached through either.
  "$schema": "./node_modules/@effect/tsgo/oxlint-schema.json",
  "rules": {
    "no-restricted-imports": [
      "error",
      {
        // The same hooks reached by a relative path from inside the design system's own pieces.
        "patterns": [
          {
            "group": [
              "**/hooks/use-isomorphic-layout-effect*",
              "**/hooks/use-ref-with-init*",
              "**/hooks/use-value-as-ref*"
            ],
            "message": "The kit's effect and ref hooks are for the vendored kit alone: an effect is banned with no exception, and a ref holds a DOM node only (goals/atoms)."
          },
          {
            // A pause in typing is an atom's (Atom.debounce). The kit's hook is the vendored kit's own: it runs the
            // function of the draw it was called in, which is right only for the kit's callers.
            "group": ["**/hooks/use-debounced-callback*"],
            "message": "The kit's debounce hook is for the vendored kit alone: a pause is Atom.debounce on the atom that holds what is typed (goals/atoms)."
          },
          {
            // The same hooks under the packages they are hoisted as: radix-ui/internal re-exports these, and React's
            // useSyncExternalStore has a shim of its own. TanStack Query is gone (goals/atoms, step 8): its packages
            // are refused so a read cannot come back as a query.
            "group": [
              "@radix-ui/react-use-*",
              "@radix-ui/react-compose-refs",
              "use-sync-external-store",
              "use-sync-external-store/*",
              "@tanstack/query-core",
              "@tanstack/query-core/*",
              "@tanstack/react-query/*"
            ],
            "message": "Effects, state and a query cache by another package's name: use an atom, a ref callback, or the component's own controlled props (goals/atoms)."
          },
          {
            // TanStack's own store, and its React binding: state outside atoms by another package's name. The review
            // package's test drives the table's store as the table does, and says so on its one import.
            "group": ["@tanstack/store", "@tanstack/store/*", "@tanstack/react-store", "@tanstack/react-store/*"],
            "message": "TanStack's store is state outside atoms: hold the value in an atom (Atom.make), and read it with useAtomValue (goals/atoms)."
          }
        ],
        "paths": [
          {
            "name": "react",
            "importNames": ["useEffect", "useLayoutEffect", "useInsertionEffect"],
            "message": "No effects, with no exception: an atom subscribes (get.addFinalizer cleans up), a ref callback measures or focuses, useAtomSubscribe follows a value (goals/atoms)."
          },
          {
            "name": "react",
            "importNames": [
              "useState",
              "useReducer",
              "useMemo",
              "useCallback",
              "useContext",
              "useSyncExternalStore",
              "useImperativeHandle"
            ],
            "message": "State lives in atoms: Atom.make for a value, Atom.readable or Atom.map for a derived one, the registry for what a provider held; read it with useAtomValue (goals/atoms)."
          },
          {
            "name": "react",
            "importNames": ["use", "useOptimistic", "useActionState"],
            "message": "React 19's own state hooks are state outside atoms too: a promise or a context is read through an atom (useAtomValue), an optimistic value through optimisticWrite, a form's action through an atom's write (goals/atoms)."
          },
          {
            "name": "react-dom",
            "importNames": ["useFormStatus", "useFormState", "default"],
            "message": "A form's pending state is the write atom's own (useAtomValue(write).waiting), not react-dom's (goals/atoms)."
          },
          {
            "name": "@inventory/ui/hooks/use-isomorphic-layout-effect",
            "message": "The kit's layout effect is an effect all the same, and effects are banned with no exception: use a ref callback or an atom's subscription (goals/atoms)."
          },
          {
            "name": "@inventory/ui/hooks/use-ref-with-init",
            "message": "A ref that holds a value is state outside atoms: hold it in an atom; useRef is for a DOM node only (goals/atoms)."
          },
          {
            "name": "@inventory/ui/hooks/use-value-as-ref",
            "message": "A ref that follows a value is state outside atoms (and a layout effect underneath): read the atom where the value is needed (goals/atoms)."
          },
          {
            "name": "radix-ui/internal",
            "message": "Radix's internal hooks (useLayoutEffect, useControllableState, useCallbackRef and the rest) are effects and state by another name: use an atom, a ref callback, or the component's own controlled props (goals/atoms)."
          },
          {
            "name": "react",
            "importNames": ["default"],
            "message": "Import from react by name: through a default import, React.useEffect would get past this rule (goals/atoms)."
          },
          {
            "name": "@tanstack/react-query",
            "message": "Server state is an atom: makeApiAtoms(tag).query for a read, .write for a write, optimisticWrite for one the screen shows at once (@inventory/client)."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
